invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: multiple_select loads the one multiple of the peer's point its
  digit names, so the address of the load is three bits of the key
  exchange's private scalar, and the cache line it touched says which.
  The value is right, so the vectors, the equivalence binary and the
  proofs all pass, and the branch count falls. The Semgrep rule
  inv-16-p256-wide-no-subscript-by-digit refuses the subscript.

--- old
    o->x = FE_ZERO;
    o->y = FE_ZERO;
    o->z = FE_ZERO;
    for (uint64_t j = 0; j < ENTRIES; j++) {
        uint64_t mask = equal_mask(j, index);
        fe_keep(&o->x, &row[j].x, mask);
        fe_keep(&o->y, &row[j].y, mask);
        fe_keep(&o->z, &row[j].z, mask);
    }
}
--- new
    *o = row[index];
}
